nly at the points corresponding to $t=-1,\\frac{2}{3}.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(-1) & =⟨4(-1)-(-1)^{2},(-1)^{3}⟩=⟨-5,-1⟩ \\\\ r(\\frac{2}{3}) & =⟨4(\\frac{2}{3})-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2},{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{3}⟩=⟨\\frac{20}{9},\\frac{8}{27}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨2,1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the points $(-5,-1)$ and $(\\frac{20}{9},\\frac{8}{27}).$"]]}]